---
import LandingPage from "../layouts/LandingPage.astro";
import { articleJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";
import { APP_URL } from "../lib/config";

const UPDATED = "2026-08-09";
const canonical = "/flown-alternative";
const title = "A FLOWN Alternative: Refocus vs FLOWN";
const description =
  "Looking for a FLOWN alternative? An honest Refocus vs FLOWN comparison — facilitated deep-work sessions and wellbeing content vs simple, free matched focus sessions.";

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What is FLOWN and why look for an alternative?",
    answer:
      "FLOWN is a deep-work membership platform with facilitated focus sessions, 24/7 drop-in rooms, and wellbeing content like breathwork and planning workshops. It's rich but membership-based, so people look for an alternative when they want something simpler and free, without the facilitator-led format or the broader curriculum.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is Refocus a free alternative to FLOWN?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Refocus is free to start with no credit card, and it focuses on one thing: matched, timed coworking sessions. FLOWN runs on a membership (with a free trial), which makes sense for its facilitated sessions and wellbeing programming but is more than some people need.",
  },
  {
    question: "Does Refocus have facilitated or guided sessions like FLOWN?",
    answer:
      "No, and that's the main difference. FLOWN offers facilitator-led 1–2 hour sessions plus guided breaks. Refocus is deliberately lightweight: you pick a 25, 50, or 75-minute session, get matched with a partner, and work — no facilitator, no curriculum, no scheduling around events.",
  },
  {
    question: "Refocus vs FLOWN — which should I choose?",
    answer:
      "Choose FLOWN if you want structured, facilitator-led deep-work sessions plus wellbeing content and are happy with a membership. Choose Refocus if you want a free, no-frills way to get matched with a focus partner in seconds and just start working.",
  },
];

const article = articleJsonLd({
  headline: title,
  description,
  path: canonical,
  dateModified: UPDATED,
});
---

<LandingPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  heading="A FLOWN alternative: Refocus vs FLOWN"
  lead="FLOWN is a polished deep-work membership with facilitated sessions and wellbeing content. It's great — but it's also more (and more expensive) than some people want. If you just need a simple, free way to focus alongside someone, here's how Refocus compares."
  updated={UPDATED}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Try Refocus free"
  ctaText="Refocus is a virtual coworking room: pick a 25, 50, or 75-minute session, get matched with someone who's also there to focus, and work side by side with synced timers. Free to start, no card required."
  ctaHref={`${APP_URL}/auth/sign-up`}
  ctaLabel="Start a free session"
  jsonLd={[article, faqJsonLd(faqs)]}
>
  <p>
    <a href="https://flown.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">FLOWN</a>
    is a deep-work platform built around
    <a href="/virtual-coworking">virtual coworking</a> and
    <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a>. Alongside 24/7 silent drop-in
    rooms, it offers facilitator-led focus sessions, peer-hosted sessions, and
    "recharge" content like breathwork, journaling, and planning workshops. It's
    a thoughtful, well-rounded membership — closer to a deep-work club than a
    single-purpose tool.
  </p>
  <p>
    That breadth is exactly why some people look for a FLOWN alternative: they
    don't want a facilitator, a curriculum, or a membership — they just want to
    sit down and focus with someone else present. That's where Refocus fits.
  </p>

  <h2>Refocus vs FLOWN at a glance</h2>
  <div class="blog-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>&nbsp;</th>
          <th>Refocus</th>
          <th>FLOWN</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Core idea</th>
          <td>Simple matched coworking sessions</td>
          <td>Deep-work membership + wellbeing content</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Session format</th>
          <td>25, 50, 75 min, self-serve, matched instantly</td>
          <td>Drop-in rooms + facilitator-led 1–2 hr sessions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Facilitators</th>
          <td>No — you and a partner, no host</td>
          <td>Yes — expert-led sessions and workshops</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Extras</th>
          <td>Synced timers, friends, global chat</td>
          <td>Breathwork, journaling, planning, community events</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Pricing</th>
          <td>Free to start, no card required</td>
          <td>Membership (free trial, no card to start)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Check FLOWN's
    <a href="https://flown.com/how-it-works" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">how-it-works</a>
    and
    <a href="https://flown.com/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">pricing</a>
    pages for their current details.
  </p>

  <h2>Where Refocus is different</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus does one thing on purpose: it gets you into a focused session with a
    partner as fast as possible. There's no facilitator to schedule around and
    nothing to learn — pick a length, get matched, work. For a lot of people the
    friction of a broader platform is the reason they never actually start, and
    a smaller surface area helps.
  </p>

  <h2>Where FLOWN is still great</h2>
  <p>
    If you value structure and variety, FLOWN is excellent. Facilitator-led
    sessions add real accountability, the recharge content supports sustainable
    focus, and there's independent research on its impact for ADHD and remote
    workers. For people who want a whole deep-work practice rather than a quick
    session, the membership earns its keep.
  </p>

  <h2>Who should pick which</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Pick FLOWN</strong> if you want facilitated sessions, wellbeing
      content, and a structured community, and a membership is fine.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pick Refocus</strong> if you want a free, instant, no-frills focus
      partner and nothing else to manage.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Weighing other options? See our
    <a href="/focusmate-alternative">Focusmate</a> and
    <a href="/cofocus-alternative">Cofocus</a> comparisons too.
  </p>
</LandingPage>
